\newlabel{sec:method}{{3}{3}{Method}{section.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Overview of TimeMorph. The temporal branch extracts ordered patch-level dynamics from the raw one-dimensional sequence, while the morphology branch converts the same sequence into a two-dimensional morphology map and extracts shape-oriented tokens with a frozen vision backbone. The two token sequences are fused and projected into the embedding space of a pretrained causal LLM. Prediction is performed by closed-set class-token scoring over dataset-specific valid labels. The training schedule contains Stage I representation pretraining, Stage II embedding-space alignment pretraining, Stage III optional label-semantic calibration, and target adaptation with warm-up and joint adaptation phases. }}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{4}{Overview of TimeMorph. The temporal branch extracts ordered patch-level dynamics from the raw one-dimensional sequence, while the morphology branch converts the same sequence into a two-dimensional morphology map and extracts shape-oriented tokens with a frozen vision backbone. The two token sequences are fused and projected into the embedding space of a pretrained causal LLM. Prediction is performed by closed-set class-token scoring over dataset-specific valid labels. The training schedule contains Stage I representation pretraining, Stage II embedding-space alignment pretraining, Stage III optional label-semantic calibration, and target adaptation with warm-up and joint adaptation phases}{figure.1}{}}
